    {
      "id": 230410,
      "name": "bolnerap",
      "username": "bolnerap",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-05-02T01:55:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint at 6 / 13 / 17 / 19 / 5.</p>\n<p>Tempest - mostly damage and card draw. I threw out Localized Hurricane and had him go to town trying to get good stuff. Ended up with a couple Chain Lightnings that I saved to pound Chokepoint later. Got good use out of a Dynamic Siphon being pinged by Writhe a couple times to keep laying on the Hurricane, and a Siphon hit from Leviathan helped end the game with Tempest using his base power to pile on more damage (and enable Fixer...).</p>\n<p>Sky-Scraper - plopped a Micro-Assembler on Writhe, then kept swapping back and forth from Tiny to Normal to use Tiny's power for damage and do a couple plinks with Proportionist.</p>\n<p>Fixer - Driving Mantis. Got a Cosmic Weapon on CC's second turn&nbsp;and got to use it a couple times, the second with a Crowbar. But mostly he sat and redirected damage. Had to take a Ball Lightning to the face on the final environment turn so he could then redirect the Leviathan hit for the final blow.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Capt. Cosmic - only used his base power turn 1. Otherwise, it was plenty useful to just play the Crest,&nbsp;Weapon, and Siphon in that order. He blocked so much damage that I didn't want to risk losing his constructs by using his base power.</p>\n<p>Writhe - Cloak/Siphon turn 1, then he lost the Cloak to being destroyed by Shocking Animation and that was that. But Umbral Siphon did WORK, and he was able to ping the Siphon with card plays besides.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:05:23.797Z",
